diff --git a/docs/utils.rst b/docs/utils.rst
index 995c171..0f3b63b 100644
--- a/docs/utils.rst
+++ b/docs/utils.rst
@@ -212,11 +212,18 @@ Example usage::
 Alternatively, the function can also be used to launch editors for files by
 a specific filename.  In this case, the return value is always `None`.
 
+One editor session can open multiple files by passing an iterable of
+filenames.  Each filename is passed as a distinct literal argument,
+including names containing whitespace or shell metacharacters.  An empty
+iterable or an item that is not a string is rejected before the editor starts.
+
 Example usage::
 
     import click
     click.edit(filename='/etc/passwd')
 
+    click.edit(filename=['notes.txt', 'release notes.txt'])
+
 
 Launching Applications
 ----------------------
